From 6ee867a4714a0ea951a65029918c26a38eed3462 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:59:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] perf: floating windows move together with the rest; every
 question to the window system is counted

A layout foretold only the moves of docked windows (`WindowSystem.moveTogether`), so on a desk with floating
windows each of those waited for its app on its own. Now `placeFloatingWindows` makes its plan, foretells from that
very plan, and walks it. Not together with the docked windows: floating windows are placed last, after the rounds in
which a window that refuses its slot has the layout reckoned again, and the Desktop may be elsewhere by then.

The fake counts every question it is asked, by name (`asked`). `Budget` has `questions` and `windowLists`: the three
questions that have the window server list every window there is. A command asks for one such list at most; an app
that quits and a start may ask for more, and the test says why. `arbor-sim bench` prints the table.
What was left of a layout's first forecast when the second came is counted as unclaimed too.

`Workload` keeps the docked groups of a desk of so many windows: a benchmark makes hundreds of the same.
