From cf8d6c8864f410507832676755cbde49fe42d233 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 01:24:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] test: nets for forecasts: twin Macs on random walks, a
 chaos rule, and a trial that foretells nothing

With two forecasts in a layout, the second drops what is left of the first, so the long walk in `MoveTogetherTests`, which looked
only at what the last forecast had left, no longer saw a docked window moved for nothing. It looks at both now.

The fake took a forecast at one frame followed by a request for another for a claim: the window went to two places and nothing
counted it but `repeatMoves`, where somebody looked for that. It is unclaimed now (`forecastsNobodyClaimed`, which names the windows).

A drop that is only tried out (`reflowWhileDragging`) foretells nothing, as before this branch: the trial and its layout are lent to
`placeFloatingWindows` meanwhile, and a forecast begins with a report of what was left of the one before.

New: the chaos test's rule `forecast` (no window is moved ahead of a request that never comes), also after a step that ends with
Arbor paused or gone, with a test that it can fail; `onRandomWalksTakingTheHintChangesNothingEither`: one Mac takes the hint, its
twin ignores it, both are done the same random things to, and after every step they must be the same; it also says how much was
foretold, so that it cannot pass by foretelling nothing. Tried against five mutants (floating windows foretold from the layout as
first reckoned; at the size they have where they shrink out of view; though they are in place; a docked misfit foretold; a trial
that foretells): each turns a test red.

The commands that may ask for more than one list of all windows do ask for as many, or `whatMayAskForMoreListsDoes` fails.
The fake's own look-ups are nobody's question; `isHolding` is one. The table in `arbor-sim bench` has a column for every question
that was asked, on a desk of the sizes given. The census knows the fake's new members.
