From 61225ea7f2edda92e786b9c3b1ce44d03a2c43e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ebg-ant <296364998+ebg-ant@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 06:37:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] fix: a docked window that has answered where it belongs
 is not foretold

A window of which it is not known whether it takes its slot's size is asked where it stands. If that is also where its answer belongs,
`place` asks nothing more of it. Both forecasts of docked moves foretold a request all the same: "stay as you are", a call to its app for
nothing, which nobody then claimed. One function now says what `place` asks first (`whatPlaceAsksFirst`), and both go by it: the
forecast before `apply`, and the one in the middle of it for the windows that were asked whether they can grow.

Found by the twins on random walks, in five of two thousand, as soon as the rule about forecasts met that way of asking. The real
window system does not hear forecasts yet, so nobody has met it. Two scripts, shrunk, are tests; 2,700 walks since find nothing.
